1. Parties and definitions

"Maintainer" means the person who controls the GitHub account @AZgunNut,
or that person's lawful successor as owner of the covered ShopAI rights.

"Covered Work" means original ShopAI code and documentation published in
the AZgunNut/ShopAI-Open repository, but ONLY to the extent the Maintainer
has sufficient rights to grant permissions under this license.

"ShopAI-Based Work" means software, an application, an agent, a service,
a modified version, or a distributed component that copies, modifies,
incorporates, or is legally derived from any part of the Covered Work.
Changing names, moving code to another repository, combining it with
other components, or changing the programming language does not avoid
these terms where the resulting work still contains or derives from
copyright-protected portions of the Covered Work. Mere independent
interoperability, ideas, functionality, and unrelated code are not
automatically covered.

"Commercial Use" includes using a ShopAI-Based Work in a business,
for paid work, for internal business operations, in a paid or
revenue-supported product, or in a commercial hosted service,
whether or not the software itself is sold.

"Corresponding ShopAI Source" means the preferred human-editable
source code for the portions of a ShopAI-Based Work copied or derived
from the Covered Work, including modifications, integration code
necessary to use those modifications, relevant configuration/build
instructions, and a list of third-party dependencies. It does not
include unrelated independently developed code, third-party material
the licensee has no right to disclose, private credentials, customer
data, model weights, or infrastructure secrets.

2. Ownership and third-party rights

The Maintainer licenses only material for which the Maintainer has
