3. Free personal use

You may download, inspect, copy, run, fork, modify, and share the
Covered Work for personal, educational, hobby, and other noncommercial
purposes, free of license fees, subject to Sections 2, 5, and 7.

Purely private, noncommercial modifications need not be disclosed.

If you publish or distribute a noncommercial modified version,
you must notify the Maintainer as described in Section 5 and make
its Corresponding ShopAI Source available at no charge to the
Maintainer under Section 6.

4. Commercial use is permitted with reciprocity

You may copy, modify, integrate, run, distribute, sell, and provide
the Covered Work or a ShopAI-Based Work commercially without paying
the Maintainer a license fee, PROVIDED that you comply with all of
these conditions and pass along applicable notices and this license:

a. You identify ShopAI as a source component or basis, retain
   copyright and license notices, and identify your changes.

b. For each commercial ShopAI-Based Work, including an internal
   business implementation or hosted service, you give the
   Maintainer a complete copy of its Corresponding ShopAI Source
   and reasonable build/use instructions, at no charge, within
   30 days of its first Commercial Use or release. Supply updated
   Corresponding ShopAI Source within 30 days of each material
   subsequent commercial version or release. Source may be
   delivered privately; this license does not require posting
   commercial source publicly.

c. You grant the Maintainer a perpetual, worldwide, nonexclusive,
   irrevocable (as to delivered versions), royalty-free, fully
   paid-up license to use, run, copy, modify, test, maintain,
   compile, and create derivative works from that Corresponding
   ShopAI Source, for the Maintainer's own personal OR commercial
   purposes, with no license fee, subscription, royalty, or
   revenue-sharing obligation to you. This grant includes the
   right to use improvements in the Maintainer's own ShopAI
   versions, but does not automatically grant rights to
   unrelated third-party material.

d. If you offer a commercial ShopAI-Based software product,
   downloadable release, or hosted software service to customers
   or users, you must also provide the Maintainer, on request,
   with free-of-charge, ongoing use of the ShopAI-Based software
   functionality you commercially offer, including the
   corresponding paid software features and version updates.
   For hosted services, provide an account or equivalent access
   at no subscription/license charge, subject only to ordinary
   technical safeguards and reasonable anti-abuse limits.
   This obligation concerns the ShopAI-Based software or service
   and does not require gifting physical hardware, paid
   third-party services or unrelated products.

e. These reciprocal rights and no-fee access obligations apply
   to commercial ShopAI-Based Works whether they are marketed as
   ShopAI, rebranded, sold as part of a larger product, or
   provided as a service. They do not extend to independently
   written products that do not contain or legally derive from
   the Covered Work.

5. How to notify and share versions

Notify the Maintainer through the GitHub Issues page at:
https://github.com/AZgunNut/ShopAI-Open/issues

Give the project/version name, a short change summary, and a
public source link when available. If a commercial version's
source is not public, use an Issue to request a PRIVATE delivery
method; do not post secrets, private customer data, or
proprietary source into a public issue. The Maintainer may
provide a reasonable secure receiving method.

Noncommercial published versions should be notified within
30 days of publication. Commercial versions follow the
30-day timing in Section 4(b).

